= Enzyme — Simple =

An '''enzyme''' is a molecule that helps a chemical reaction happen faster.

Most enzymes are proteins. Some RNA molecules can also act as enzymes. Each enzyme works with particular reactants and conditions.

Enzymes help cells carry out chemical reactions without needing extreme temperatures. They can be used repeatedly, but their activity depends on conditions such as temperature and acidity.

An enzyme can speed up a reaction without changing which mixture would be at [[Chemical equilibrium|equilibrium]].

